    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "ec_pubkey_combine: return early if a public key fails to load",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "When the illegal callback does not abort, `secp256k1_ec_pubkey_combine` returns 1 even if one of its input public keys is invalid, because it ignores the result of `secp256k1_pubkey_load`. This PR makes it return 0 in that case. #1919 adds the same check to `secp256k1_ecdh`.\n\nThis is only the minimal check. It does not settle the discussion in #1872 on whether `secp256k1_pubkey_load` should return `void`, where `_pubkey_combine` is named as one of the callers that ignore its result. The new test passes a zeroed public key at each position of the input array and expects the illegal callback to fire and the call to return 0. It fails on master and passes with the change.\n",
